        <detaileddescription>
<para>Load Step Plugin.</para>
<para>Calls <computeroutput>themis_create_step()</computeroutput> from the .so/.dll. If <computeroutput>manifest</computeroutput> is provided, the library path and MIME type are validated before dlopen() (§Phase 3 DLL sandbox).</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>plugin_name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Logical name to register the plugin under. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>library_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Absolute filesystem path to the shared library. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>manifest</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Optional sandbox constraints. Empty manifest (default) permits any path and MIME type. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Error when the library cannot be loaded, the entry point is missing, or sandbox validation fails.</para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">plugin_name</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Name of the plugin. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">library_path</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Path to the library. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">manifest</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Input parameter. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Return value.</para>
</simplesect>
Calls: empty(), fs::weakly_canonical(), string(), rfind(), tl::make_unexpected(), sf(), is_open(), json::parse(). </para>
